### The body-shaped collection read (#107), against real PostgreSQL in the container.
### Every fact below pairs the body with the query string that means the same thing, because the
### claim this route makes is not "it answers" but "it answers WHAT THE URL ANSWERS" — and only a
### real engine can show that the transposed parameters reached the same statement.

### A filter, a sort and a page size, sent as a body
# @name BodyGroupOrderLimit
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders/query
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "or": "(status.eq.completed,status.eq.cancelled)",
  "order": "reference.asc",
  "limit": "100"
}

### The same read as a query string, which is the control the comparison needs
# @name UrlGroupOrderLimit
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?or=(status.eq.completed,status.eq.cancelled)&order=reference.asc&limit=100
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

### A projection with an alias, through the body
# @name BodyAliasedProjection
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders/query
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "select": "ref:reference,status", "order": "reference.asc", "limit": "100" }

### An empty object is the empty query: every readable field, the default page
# @name BodyEmptyQuery
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders/query
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### The tenant boundary holds on this route too: the SOUTH dispatcher asking for a NORTH row by name
# @name BodyOtherTenantByName
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders/query
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherSouth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reference": "eq.WO-1001", "limit": "100" }

### The same body from the row's own tenant, which is what makes the empty page above mean something
# @name BodyOwnTenantByName
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders/query
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reference": "eq.WO-1001", "limit": "100" }

### A field this caller may not read is refused exactly as an undeclared name is
# @name BodyMaskedField
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [422]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders/query
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "internal_notes": "eq.anything" }

### ...and the undeclared name it must be indistinguishable from
# @name BodyUndeclaredField
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [422]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders/query
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "no_such_field_at_all": "eq.anything" }
